**Tempting reading:** The Defense Science Board is a federal advisory committee made up largely of outside experts, so subsection (i) looks like outside participation. That reading fails against the definition. The Board only does an annual review of "progress" and reports its findings. It does not give input before any federal decision, which makes it like the study consultation in Example 3. Every other interaction in the section stays inside the federal government:
- the collaboration with the Office of the National Coordinator (part of HHS);
- the Executive Committee, whose members are all appointed from within DoD and VA;
- the briefings, reports, certifications and notifications to congressional committees;
- the Comptroller General's assessment.
